 fine="General information only. Lenders set final approval. Not mortgage advice.",
 cap="Milton buyers: you may not need 20% down.\n\nThe minimum down payment in Canada is 5% of the first $500,000 of the price plus 10% of the part from $500,000 up to $1.5 million (20% at $1.5 million or more). On a $700,000 home that is $25,000 + $20,000 = $45,000, compared with $140,000 for 20%. With less than 20% down you will typically need mortgage loan insurance, which adds a cost, and your lender still checks your income, credit and the home.\nSource: Financial Consumer Agency of Canada (canada.ca). Confirm with your lender.\n\nWant help planning your budget? "+INFO+"\n\nGeneral information only. Not mortgage advice.",
